  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of Inclusive Cross-Border Governance and Strengthening the Resilience of Populations in the Border Areas of Mauritania and Senegal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scheduled over a period of twenty-four (24) months, the project aims to mitigate security risks and promote social cohesion in the border areas of Mauritania and Senegal.The project will focus on (3) complimentary strategic axes which ensure its coherence: (i)- Strengthening of cross-border governance with a view to guaranteeing border security and preventing illicit cross-border trafficking; (ii) Strengthening of confidence between border populations and the central State, on the one hand, and between cross-border communities, on the other hand, with a view to consolidating social cohesion and reducing tensions in the border areas of Mauritania and Senegal; (iii) Strengthening the resilience of populations through access to basic social services and the empowerment of young people through capacity building in the prevention of transnational organized crime. Moreover, taking into account the interconnection between these factors, the project intends to build on the existing situation by favoring strategic partnerships with regional entities -Senegal River Development Organization, West African Economic and Monetary Union- or even research centers - Institute for Security Studies -, thus making it possible to combine mobilization of additional potential and a better perspective understanding of the dynamics involved.</narrative>
  </description>
